implementationPlan.description:
ONE GOAL REACHES A RUNNING ENVIRONMENT (DoD 2) — needs docker; skip to step 6 and block if step 1 found none.

In `tests/e2e/foundation/platform-pipeline.e2e.test.ts`, drive the whole pipeline on ONE goal, each link through the REAL path its band ships:
1. scaffold a repository from a PRD (the controlled-profile generator, landed at sha 2feed27b, emits a 22-file tree);
2. deploy it at a landed sha;
3. set its variables and prove they reach the process;
4. migrate its schema;
5. probe its health.

ASSERT THE DEPLOYED THING SERVES. DoD 2 is explicit: an HTTP RESPONSE from the running environment, NOT a receipt saying it should be up. A receipt asserts intent; a response asserts reality, and the entire point of an epic-final row is to tell those apart. Name the sha and quote the probe result.

Assert the served build corresponds to the LANDED SHA — not merely that something answers on the port. Something answering is compatible with a stale container from a previous run, which is exactly the confusion a leaked resource creates.

MOCK NOTHING IN THE CHAIN (rail 1). Doubles are permitted only outside it — a clock, an external registry. Name each and why it is not a link.

Reuse the real-process harness shape from tests/e2e/foundation/ (e2e-harness.ts, j1-loop-harness.ts) rather than inventing a fifth. Teardown in a `finally`, and step 5 will verify it actually happened.

THE DOCS SWEEP AND THE COMPLETION RECORD (DoD 6, second half) — no docker needed.

DOCS, in ONE pass, held back from the individual rows so the same file is not re-edited five times: the operator-facing words for ALL FIVE bands (repository, deploy, secrets, migrations, monitoring) and any doc that still describes the platform as unbuilt. Read `docs/agent-stack-runbook.md`, `README.md` and `docs/VISION.md` — VISION:141 lists Stage 2 as "repository bootstrapping; infrastructure generation; preview and production deployment; secrets and environment management; database migrations; monitoring, backup, and rollback; release evidence".

MARK SHIPPED ONLY WHAT THIS ROW ACTUALLY PROVED. If step 1 blocked on docker, say so in the docs: the machinery is verified and the live pipeline is pending a docker host. Overstating Stage 2 retires questions no one has answered, and this is the one row whose docs a reader will trust as the platform's status. If a doc needed no change, name the files you READ.

COMPLETION RECORD — state explicitly:
- which DoD items were met and which are blocked, with the docker output verbatim if blocked;
- the canary's SHAPE and the exact paths swept;
- the adversarial pass's checklist and findings;
- the path-attributed baseline (step 2's run vs the final run, subtracted, intersected with owned paths) — complete only when that intersection is EMPTY.

The verification command recorded on `moe.complete_task` is `pnpm --filter @moe/daemon test`. If the row blocks instead, `moe.report_blocked` carries the same evidence plus the measurable unblock condition from step 1.
